# wallet-rescue

> **Recover lost Bitcoin, Electrum and Bitcoin Core wallets, private keys and seed phrases
> from a raw `dd`/`ddrescue` disk image — even when the filesystem is destroyed, formatted or
> overwritten.** Offline, forensic, zero false positives.

**Python 3.8+** · **Linux** · **Offline** · **Zero false positives**

`wallet-rescue` scans the **raw byte stream** of a disk image, block device or mounted
filesystem and carves out Bitcoin key material — WIF private keys, extended keys, Bitcoin Core
`wallet.dat` records, Electrum wallets of **every version**, BIP39 and Electrum seed phrases,
and DER-encoded EC keys (pywallet-style). Every hit is **structurally validated**, encrypted
wallets are **tested against your own password list**, and recovered addresses can be
**balance-checked** on-chain.

